<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pol Pot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1925">1925</a>–<a href="/years/1998">1998</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Saloth Sar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pol Pot was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> and of Democratic Kampuchea from 1975 to 1979. His regime emptied the cities, abolished money and religion, and forced the population into rural labour camps, causing the deaths of some 1.5 to 2 million Cambodians by execution, starvation and disease. A Vietnamese invasion overthrew him in 1979, and he died in the jungle in 1998.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pol-pot.jpg" alt="Pol Pot" width="320" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Editura Politică · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pol_Pot_in_1978.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Pol Pot was born Saloth Sâr in the village of Prek Sbauv, outside Kampong Thom, the son of a prosperous farmer. He was educated at some of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>'s most elite schools, boarding from 1942 at a new junior middle school in Kampong Cham, where fellow pupils such as Hu Nim and Khieu Samphan later served in his government. He arrived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> on 1 October 1949 on a scholarship to study radio electronics, and joined the French Communist Party in 1951. He returned to Cambodia in 1953 and worked with the Khmer Việt Minh, then taught in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phnom-penh">Phnom Penh</a> while remaining a central figure in the Marxist-Leninist movement.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Career</h2><p>In 1959 the movement was formalised as the Kampuchean Labour Party, later renamed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Communist Party of Kampuchea</a>. To avoid repression by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Norodom Sihanouk</a>'s government, Pol Pot moved to a jungle camp in 1962, and in February 1963 he was elected party secretary. The war against Sihanouk was launched in January 1968. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lon-nol">Lon Nol</a> deposed Sihanouk in March 1970, Sihanouk allied with the Khmer Rouge, and his support greatly helped recruitment. In May 1973 Pol Pot ordered the collectivisation of villages in Khmer Rouge territory. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phnom-penh">Phnom Penh</a> fell on 17 April 1975, and he secretly entered the abandoned city three days later.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">In office</h2><p>In January 1976 a new constitution renamed the country Democratic Kampuchea. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> emptied the cities and moved the urban population to collective farms and labour camps, where mass executions, torture, malnutrition and disease were rampant. Money, religion and private property were abolished, and more than 1.3 million people were executed and buried in mass graves. After repeated border clashes and massacres of Vietnamese villagers, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> launched a full-scale invasion on 25 December 1978, and by January 1979 the Khmer Rouge were toppled.</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> retreated to the jungles near the Thai border and kept fighting until the Vietnamese withdrew in 1989. In June 1997 Pol Pot ordered the killing of Son Sen, which prompted the commander Ta Mok to turn against him. Pol Pot was placed under house arrest and died shortly afterward in 1998. Some Cambodians still leave offerings at his grave in Anlong Veng, while many call the period samai a-Pot, the era of the contemptible Pot.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Pol Pot” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In July 1963 <b>Pol Pot</b> and most of the communist central committee set up an insurgent base in Ratanakiri among the Khmer Loeu, and the Khmer Rouge insurgency began in 1967–68.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970">Kingdom of Cambodia (1953-1970) · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Khmer Rouge, a Maoist movement under <b>Pol Pot</b>, abolished money and private property and emptied Phnom Penh, and its Killing Fields caused the deaths of 2,700,000 people by mass murder and genocide.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/marxism-leninism">Marxism–Leninism · In Power</a></li><li><blockquote>Its title refers to 17 April 1975, the day the Khmer Rouge came to power in Cambodia and set up a communist dictatorship of Maoist inspiration under <b>Pol Pot</b>.</blockquote><a href="/songs/dap-prampi-mesa-moha-chouk-chey">Dap Prampi Mesa Moha Chouk Chey</a></li><li><blockquote>Vietnam's army took the Cambodian capital, ending <b>Pol Pot</b>'s regime, under which some 1.5 to 2 million people had died.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-7">7 January in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The regime, led by <b>Pol Pot</b>, emptied the cities, abolished money, markets, schools and religion, and forced the population into agricultural communes.</blockquote><a href="/state/democratic-kampuchea">Democratic Kampuchea</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Prek Sbauv, in what is now <a href="/countries/cambodia">Cambodia</a>. Died in Anlong Veng District, in what is now <a href="/countries/cambodia">Cambodia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=12.7,104.9&amp;year=1972" aria-label="Prek Sbauv on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7430 1690 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Pol Pot"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7880 1960h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7880 1960h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=12.7,104.9&amp;year=1972">What was here in 1972? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
